# ⚠️  THERE ARE TWO APPLE ACCOUNTS ON THIS MACHINE. SAY WHICH ONE THIS IS.
#
# ZKProofport ships from Masse Labs Inc. A key from any other Apple account
# will authenticate fine and then show you a different app list — on 2026-08-29
# the local .env.ios held a key from an unrelated account, and
# com.masselabs.zkproofport looked like it did not exist.
#
# The failure is quiet: no permission error, just an app that is not there.
# Before trusting a local upload, list the apps the key can see and confirm
# com.masselabs.zkproofport is among them.
#
# The corporate credentials used by CI live in GitHub secrets on
# zkproofport/proofport-app (ASC_KEY_ID / ASC_ISSUER_ID / ASC_API_KEY).

# App Store Connect API Key for TestFlight uploads
#
# Create at: https://appstoreconnect.apple.com/access/integrations/api
#   1. Click "+" to generate a new key
#   2. Name: "ZKProofport CI" (or any name)
#   3. Access: "App Manager" role (minimum for TestFlight uploads)
#   4. Download the .p8 file (only downloadable ONCE!)
#
# Fill in these values:

# Key ID: shown in the API Keys list (e.g., "ABC1234DEF")
export ASC_KEY_ID=""

# Issuer ID: shown at the top of the API Keys page (UUID format)
export ASC_ISSUER_ID=""

# API Key: base64-encode the .p8 file content
#   Run: base64 -i AuthKey_XXXXXXXX.p8 | tr -d '\n'
export ASC_API_KEY=""
